      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humble%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first oil refinery, Humble Oil & Refining Company, opened in 1911 and later became part of Exxon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humble%2C_Texas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Railroad tracks reached Humble in 1904, and the first tank car of oil left the town’s field the next year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humble%2C_Texas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The DeLorean Motor Company’s only remaining private factory, famous for the Back to the Future car, sits in Humble.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
